 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "I'd like ~ / Can I have ~? (공손한 요청)",
   "en": "I'd like ~ / Can I have ~? (polite requests)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "주문할 때는 I'd like ~(= I would like)가 가장 공손하고 자연스럽습니다. 부탁은 Can I have ~? 로, 끝에 please를 붙이면 더 공손합니다.",
   "en": "To order, 'I'd like ~' (= I would like) is polite and natural. Ask with 'Can I have ~?' and add 'please' to be more polite."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Phrase",
    "쓰임 / Use"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I'd like ~",
     "주문 · 공손한 요청"
    ],
    [
     "Can I have ~?",
     "부탁하기"
    ],
    [
     "What would you like?",
     "주문을 받을 때"
    ],
    [
     "~, please.",
     "더 공손하게"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "I'd는 I would의 줄임말입니다.",
    "en": "I'd is short for I would."
   },
   {
    "ko": "please를 붙이면 더 공손합니다: A coffee, please.",
    "en": "Adding 'please' makes it more polite: A coffee, please."
   },
   {
    "ko": "Would you like ~?는 무언가를 권할 때 씁니다.",
    "en": "Use 'Would you like ~?' to offer something."
   }
  ],
